  "acrm---why-emergent-table": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><style>\n  .cmp--emg-first thead th.col-brand-head { background: #ebebeb; }\n  .cmp--emg-first tbody tr:nth-child(odd) td.col-brand { background: #f2f2f2; }\n  .cmp--emg-first tbody tr:nth-child(even) td.col-brand { background: #e6e6e6; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"cmp cmp--emg-first\">\n  <table>\n    <colgroup>\n      <col class=\"col-feature\" />\n      <col class=\"col-brand\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n      <col class=\"col-other\" />\n    </colgroup>\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th class=\"col-feature\" scope=\"col\"><span class=\"visually-hidden\"></span></th>\n        <th class=\"col-brand-head\" scope=\"col\">\n          <img class=\"brand-logo\" src=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6a0edf12ef1a8562ed56d806/6a0ef94db7f0a045fab57060_logo.svg\" alt=\"Emergent\" />\n        </th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Jotform</th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Google Forms</th>\n        <th scope=\"col\">Typeform</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">How you build</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">Describe it in plain English</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Templates, editor, AI generator</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Manual, field by field</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Templates, editor, AI assist</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Response limits</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">No response caps</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Monthly submission caps by plan; the form stops at the cap</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">No limit</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Monthly response caps by plan; the form closes at the cap</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Where responses live</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">A database table you own, plus any integration</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Jotform account</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Google Sheets</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">Typeform account</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th scope=\"row\">Code ownership</th>\n        <td class=\"col-brand\">Full code export to GitHub on paid plans</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n        <td class=\"col-other\">None</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div></div>",
  "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { customerFeedback: \"Build a customer feedback form for my online store. Seven days after an order is delivered, email the customer a short form with a 1 to 5 star rating and an optional comment box. If the rating is 2 stars or lower, send our support lead Dana a Slack direct message with the order number, the rating and the comment. Save every answer to the orders database.\", openHouseFeedback: \"Make an open house feedback form for my real estate listings. Visitors scan a QR code at the door and answer 3 questions on their phone: what they think of the asking price, the condition of the home and whether they are interested. Count the answers per listing and build a report I can send the seller after each open house.\", presentationFeedback: \"Create a feedback form for the workshops I run. Attendees rate clarity, pacing and usefulness on a 1 to 5 scale and can leave a comment. Close the form at the end of the day, then show me the average score for each question with the lowest one first, along with the comments for that question.\", patientFeedback: \"Set up a patient feedback form for our clinics. Two hours after each visit, email the patient a form asking how long they waited and how the staff treated them. If someone reports a wait over 30 minutes, flag the visit to the practice manager for that location with the patient's comment. Keep every answer in our database.\" };</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Feedback Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a feedback form?\", \"a\": \"A feedback form asks people to rate one experience and say what should change. It usually goes out right after a purchase or an appointment. Most pair a single rating, often 1 to 5 stars, with an optional comment box. The rating shows how it went, and the comment says why.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Pick the decision the answers will inform, then write one rating question, one or two specific questions and a comment box. Choose when it goes out and who reads the low scores. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns that description into a working form with alerts and a database.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is another term for feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Comment card is the older name, from the paper slips left on restaurant tables. People also say evaluation form or feedback survey. A survey tends to run longer and go to a planned group, while a feedback form follows one specific experience.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the different types of feedback forms?\", \"a\": \"The common split is by who answers. Customer and client feedback forms follow a purchase or a project. Talks and workshops get event forms. Clinics send one after each appointment. Inside a company, an employee feedback form asks staff about a manager or a process.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide some examples of feedback forms?\", \"a\": \"A restaurant comment card asks about the food and the service. A post-delivery form asks for a star rating and what went wrong. Coaches send a coaching feedback form after each session to ask whether it moved the client toward a goal. When a review is glowing, a testimonial form asks permission to quote it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a feedback form include?\", \"a\": \"Open with one rating, such as how satisfied the person was with the visit. Add a question about the step you control, such as delivery speed. Close with an optional comment box. Good feedback form questions ask about one thing at a time and never two in one sentence.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a customer feedback form template include?\", \"a\": \"It should carry the order or visit it refers to, pulled from the link the customer clicked. Then add a satisfaction rating and a question about the reason. A simple feedback form with those parts plus an optional comment is quick to finish on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on an open house feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Ask visitors whether they work with an agent, what they think of the asking price and how the home compares with others they have toured. Other agents tour a listing before the public at a broker open house. That broker open house feedback form should focus on price and condition.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you make a feedback form for students?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to five questions about one course or unit, and let students answer without their names. Ask what helped them learn and what they would change. Teachers can collect it at the end of each unit. A training feedback form works the same way for adult learners.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a constructive feedback form?\", \"a\": \"A constructive feedback form asks for specific observations and one concrete suggestion instead of a bare score. It suits peer reviews and talks, where the person on the receiving end wants something to work on. A presentation feedback form of this kind asks what the speaker should keep and what to cut. Requesting an example for each answer keeps the comments usable.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
